# The Hunspell dictionary is third-party data, not source. Git's line-ending
# normalisation rewrites every one of its ~50,000 lines on checkout, which
# produces noisy diffs and makes the file that ships differ byte-for-byte from
# the file that was tested. nspell tolerates CRLF today; nothing guarantees a
# future parser will.
extension/dictionaries/* -text

# Everything else is normalised to LF in the repository and checked out
# however the platform prefers.
* text=auto
